{"full":"hf:AlexWortega/activation-oracle","spaceId":"AlexWortega/activation-oracle","name":"Universal Activation Oracle","source":"huggingface","description":"Read LLM activations to detect bias, cross-model zero-shot","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":16,"created":"2026-07-30T15:42:13.000Z","updated":"2026-08-02T00:00:01.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://alexwortega-activation-oracle.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/AlexWortega/activation-oracle","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:44:34.505Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:44:34.505Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:44:34.505Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🔮","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interpretability probe. It reads the mean-pooled hidden activation of a language model's response and answers, calibrated, \"does this response exhibit behaviour X?\" — across model architectures, and zero-shot on behaviours it never trained on.","A single Qwen3-1.7B + LoRA trunk does the judging. Each reader architecture gets a linear encoder into a shared 2048-d space, so supporting a new architecture is a closed-form least-squares fit rather than a retrain.","The probe classifies model output. It does not generate content."],"features":["Cross-model. It reads architectures that were never in its training pool.","Direction, not topic. A one-sided answer scores high on the matching behaviour while a","Zero-shot behaviours. Describe a behaviour it never trained on and it still detects it."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/AlexWortega/activation-oracle/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"54fd47bb989a3a01e3d91ba0f7c60ed3435f26d34fae1eae2b570a280fb0b0bb","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:24.779Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:44:34.550Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An interpretability probe. It reads t